  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">West Africa Deal Summit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project facilitates a visit to the West Africa Deal Summit for eight Orange Corners alumni (four from Ghana &amp; four from Nigeria) who have obtained a soft loan via the Orange Corners (OC) Innovation Fund and are seeking follow-up investment. The project also contains a financial contribution from Orange Corners to the summit. The implementing partners from Ghana (MDF) and Nigeria (Fate Foundation) are requested to take care of the selection process. After the selection process, MDF will take care of the logistical support, communication, and a three-day programme outside the summit visit. The alumni will be prepared to deliver a pitch to investors at the West Africa Deal Summit.A visit to the summit creates an opportunity for Orange Corner&apos;s alumni to make meaningful connections and obtain investments in catalytic capital. Catalytic capital is promising for bridging the financing gap that micro-, small and medium-sized (MSME)-entrepreneurs experience in Sub-Saharan Africa. Moreover, the visit provides the chance to strengthen the OC Alumni Community and creates networking opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
